    "description": "Wonderful lot of two vintage 1940s illustrated children’s books featuring an especially collectible First Edition Walt Disney Fantasia title.\n\nDance of the Hours from Walt Disney’s Fantasia is clearly marked First Edition and copyright 1940 by Walt Disney Productions. Published by Harper & Brothers and printed in the United States by Western Printing and Lithographing Company. Features the colorful characters from the “Dance of the Hours” sequence of Disney’s landmark Fantasia.\n\nAlso included is Eric Knight’s classic Lassie Come-Home, illustrated by Marguerite Kirmse. This is a WWII-era Victory Book edition, printed on lighter-weight paper in accordance with War Production Board regulations. Copyright 1940 by The John C. Winston Company, with the printing history shown through the thirteenth printing, November 1943.\nBoth books show visible age and use consistent with their 1940s vintage, including cover, edge and corner wear. The colorful original cover artwork remains especially charming and displayable. Please review all photos carefully for condition and edition/printing details.",
